{
  "title": "世界停下之前，再跳一次",
  "title_en": "One More Dance Before Stillness",
  "series": "神話未完成",
  "series_en": "Myths in the Making",
  "volume": 2,
  "model": "史旺姬",
  "creator": "史旺基 Swanky",
  "slug": "swanky-ji-dance-before-stillness",
  "date": "2026-10-18",
  "count": 36,
  "cover_photo": 28,
  "setting": "紅土庭院到河階",
  "lead": "她以為世界要靠她的每一步才能轉動。",
  "lead_en": "She believed the world would turn only if she never missed a step.",
  "statement": "她以為世界要靠她的每一步才能轉動。\n\n舞王濕婆以一支舞維繫創造與消逝。她不是神，只是一位舞者，借來幾個意象：鼓聲化作腳下揚起的紅土，火環化作舞臺上的一圈燈，多重的身影交給兩盞燈投出的雙影。\n\n空曠的排練廳裡只有呼吸。紅土庭院裡越跳越快，直到腳步變重。卸下紅衣走進鏡廊，每一面鏡子都有她，沒有一面替她回答。黑石臺上，她終於坐下，聽別人的鼓。\n\n舞王的舞不能停；她學會的是，停下的那一拍也屬於節奏。一個人停手，另一個人才聽見。\n\n燈熄之後，河水照常流動。鼓留在階梯上，下一步不需要被觀看。",
  "statement_en": "She believed the world would turn only if she never missed a step.\n\nShiva Nataraja sustains creation and dissolution with a dance. She is not a god, only a dancer borrowing a few of its images: the drumbeat becomes red dust rising from her feet, the ring of fire a ring of stage lights, the many forms a pair of shadows cast by two lamps.\n\nIn the empty rehearsal hall there is only breath. In the red-earth courtyard she dances faster until her feet grow heavy. She sets the red costume aside and walks into a corridor of mirrors; every mirror holds her, and none answers for her. On the black stone platform she finally sits and listens to someone else's drum.\n\nNataraja's dance cannot stop. What she learns is that the paused beat belongs to the rhythm too: when one person stops, another can be heard.\n\nAfter the lights go out, the river keeps flowing. The drum stays on the steps, and the next step needs no audience.",
  "series_statement": "《神話未完成》\n史旺姬走進流傳至今的神話，留下它最核心的問題，讓它面對今天的生活。神話一直被講述、被使用，所以還沒有完成。",
  "series_statement_en": "Myths in the Making\nSwanky Ji steps into myths that are still being told, keeps the question at their heart, and lets it meet the life we live now. A myth that is still told and still used is not yet finished.",
  "story_zh": "故事從濕婆舞王（Shiva Nataraja）的意象出發。《Tirumantiram》第2799節將鼓、護佑的手勢、火、踩下的腳與抬起的腳，分別連結到創造、維繫、消逝、遮蔽與恩典。史密森尼博物館的圖像說明則將環繞的火環連結到毀滅與創造的循環。\n在這次改寫中，史旺姬是一位原創的女性表演者，並不扮演神祇本身。鼓聲化為腳下揚起的粉末，火環化為舞臺上的燈環，多重的身影由兩盞燈投出的雙影承擔。最大的改寫是停頓：舞王之舞維繫著世界，而她學到，停下來的那一拍也屬於節奏。\n婆羅多舞以基本步法組成段落、在空間與時間中成形的觀念，讓本書以腳步、衣褶、影子與停頓來排列節奏。書中的舞步、服裝、鼓與舞臺是跨文化的原創表演，沒有重現婆羅多舞或朱羅銅像的脈絡。",
  "story_en": "The story begins with the image of Shiva Nataraja. Verse 2799 of the Tirumantiram connects the drum, the protective gesture, the fire, the planted foot and the raised foot with creation, preservation, dissolution, concealment and grace, respectively. The Smithsonian's iconographic guide connects the surrounding ring of fire with the cycle of destruction and creation.\nIn this adaptation, Swanky Ji is an original female performer; she does not play the deity. The drumbeat becomes powder rising underfoot, the ring of flame becomes a ring of stage lights, and a pair of shadows cast by two lamps carries the sense of many presences. The largest change is the pause: the dance of Nataraja sustains the world, while she learns that a beat of stillness also belongs to rhythm.\nThe way Bharatanatyam builds passages from basic steps and shapes them in space and time led this book to arrange its rhythm through footsteps, folds of cloth, shadows and pauses. The steps, costumes, drum and stage are a cross-cultural original performance. They do not reconstruct Bharatanatyam or the context of Chola bronzes.",
  "sources_zh": "故事參考：《Tirumantiram》第九 Tantra，第2799節，B. Natarajan 英譯；史密森尼博物館〈The Iconography of Shiva Nataraja〉。舞步與節奏的創作參考另見 Narthaki 的 adavu 說明；本書的停頓與雙影為原創改寫。",
  "sources_en": "Story references: Tirumantiram, Tantra Nine, verse 2799, in B. Natarajan's English translation; the Smithsonian's The Iconography of Shiva Nataraja. Narthaki's discussion of adavu also informed the approach to steps and rhythm. The pause and paired shadows are inventions of this adaptation.",
  "chapters": [
    {
      "number": 1,
      "title": "先聽見",
      "title_en": "Before the First Beat",
      "text": "房間還沒有節拍。她先把自己的呼吸放進去。",
      "text_en": "The room has no rhythm yet. She begins with her own breathing."
    },
    {
      "number": 2,
      "title": "追上速度",
      "title_en": "Keeping Pace",
      "text": "越想追上，腳步越重。身體比她先知道。",
      "text_en": "The harder she tries to keep up, the heavier each step becomes. Her body knows first."
    },
    {
      "number": 3,
      "title": "鏡子之間",
      "title_en": "Between Mirrors",
      "text": "每一面鏡子都有她，沒有一面替她回答。",
      "text_en": "Every mirror holds her image. None can answer for her."
    },
    {
      "number": 4,
      "title": "容許空隙",
      "title_en": "Room for a Pause",
      "text": "一個人停手，另一個人才聽見。空隙也能讓節奏繼續。",
      "text_en": "One person stops, and another begins to listen. A pause can carry the rhythm onward."
    },
    {
      "number": 5,
      "title": "再跳一次",
      "title_en": "One More Dance",
      "text": "她不再追趕每一拍。她選擇在哪裡站穩，又在哪裡放手。",
      "text_en": "She no longer chases every beat. She chooses where to stand, and when to let go."
    },
    {
      "number": 6,
      "title": "把下一拍還回去",
      "title_en": "The Next Ordinary Step",
      "text": "燈熄了，河水還在流。下一步不需要被觀看。",
      "text_en": "The lights go out. The river keeps flowing. The next step needs no audience."
    }
  ],
